# The repo is normally bind-mounted at runtime, so this mainly controls what
# enters the build context. That matters a lot here: the working tree is ~5.8GB,
# almost all of it regenerable derived data, and an unfiltered context would
# make every build crawl.

.git
.gitignore

# Editor/OS cruft, and Excel's lock files (~$NAME.xlsx), which appear in banks/
# whenever a workbook is open locally.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
**/~$*
*.swp

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Regenerated derived data - all rebuilt by scripts/insights/refresh_all.py.
# The four biggest are gitignored for the same reason; insights.db alone is
# ~960MB and the inNNN_*.json analysis outputs add several GB more.
research/insights.db
research/bank_metrics.csv
research/in[0-9][0-9][0-9]_*.json
research/powerbi/

# Kept deliberately (small, and not refresh_all output): research/*.md research
# notes, research/bank_clusters*.csv, research/bank_entity_creation_dates.json,
# and research/market_data.json, which comes from fetch_market_data.py instead.

# NOT ignored, despite being generated: deliverable/ (~34MB). The `serve` target
# copies it in - it IS the thing being served - so excluding it here would
# silently produce an empty site. Rebuild it before building that target.

# Manually-fetched primary-source PDFs are transient working files, not build
# inputs - figures get transcribed into the build scripts, which are the real
# source of truth.
*.pdf

# Local agent/session scratch (also gitignored).
.claude/
.agents/
wayfinder/
HANDOFF.md
